  <h3 class="linklist">Bolex Reporter, Volume 14</h3>
  <!-- EPHEMERA and bolex reporter stuff -->
  <div id="books"> 
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltright" src="../images/reporter/14_1.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="283"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">1964</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 14, Number 1</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "So You Want to Make Movies?", 
        Geza De Rosner; "Successful Travel and Vacation Films", Jeanne Porterfield, 
        Lisa Chickering and George W. Perkins II; "Expedition Movie Making", Major 
        Mike Banks; "Down Under", Arnold R. Woodgate, ARPS; "Wild Flowers on Film", 
        Eldon Robbins; "Wildlife Movies", Carl E. Scott and Jack Swedberg; "Insects 
        in Their Natural Habitat", Peter T. Fetko; "Bolex in the Insect World", 
        Charles J. Long; "Birding with Bolex", J. Donald Sutherland; "Exposure 
        Automation", Ernst Wildi</li>
      <li class="desc">This issue features several articles on nature and wildlife 
        filming. There is also an extensive article discussing the automatic diaphragm 
        on the new Vario Switar EE lenses. The following products are introduced 
        or reviewed: The 18-5 Auto Projector; K2, S1 and P3 cameras; Vario Switar 
        36EE and 86EE lenses; Macro-Switar 50mm lens; Bolex H lightmeter; Pan 
        Cinor 85-2 Zoom Lens; Angenieux 120 w/ finder; Built-in base on new model 
        H cameras; Aluminum Carrying Case.</li>
      <li class="pp">36 pages</li>
    </ul>
    <hr>
    <ul>
      <li><img class="fltleft" src="../images/reporter/14_2.jpg" alt="Bolex Reporter" width="220" height="283"></li>
      <li class="bolrep">1964-1965</li>
      <li class="bolrep">Volume 14, Number 2</li>
      <li class="repart"><strong>Articles:</strong> "So, You Want to Make Movies! 
        Part II", Geza De Rosner; "35mm to 8mm - Closer Than You Think", Myron 
        A. Matzkin; "Shooting Rhino", Robert Citron; "Free Lancing in Alaska", 
        Harold Eastwood; "Effective 8mm Projection", Ernst Wildi; "Close-Up Filming", 
        Ted Browne; "My Bolex Feeds Eight Hungry Mouths", William Stockdale</li>
      <li class="desc">The 'Technical Corner' of this issue explains lens mounts 
        and discusses the interchangeability of Kern lenses for use with all models 
        of Bolex cameras</li>
      <li class="pp">36 pages</li>
    </ul>
